From: Noswad <64293615+TheNoswad@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] media: i2c: imx386: turn embedded data off

The imx386 sends a 640-byte Sony embedded-data line before every frame on
virtual channel 0. gs101-mipi-csis routes by virtual channel only, so the
WDMA writes it as 512 pixels: the image moves 512 pixels down the buffer
each frame, the link flags HRESOL_MISMATCH on every frame, and the WDMA
FIFO fills and stops after ~57 frames (the ultra-wide "stall"). The front
imx355 pads its embedded line to a full image line, which is why it never
drifts.

The vendor HAL writes 0x4041 = 0x00 (found in liblyric_hwl.so's imx386
register constants); with it the line is gone, HRESOL stays clear and the
ultra-wide streams continuously. Verified on oriole.
---
--- a/drivers/media/i2c/imx386.c	2026-10-13 21:06:04.198358700 -0500
+++ b/drivers/media/i2c/imx386.c	2026-10-13 21:06:04.208493751 -0500
@@ -292,6 +292,13 @@
 	{ 0x0101, 0x00 },
 	{ 0x0101, 0x03 },
 	{ 0x300b, 0x01 },
+	/*
+	 * Embedded data off, as the vendor HAL does. Otherwise a 640-byte
+	 * embedded-data line precedes every frame on VC0; the CSIS routes by
+	 * VC, so the WDMA takes it as 512 pixels, the image slips 512 pixels
+	 * per frame and the WDMA FIFO jams after ~57 frames.
+	 */
+	{ 0x4041, 0x00 },
 };
 
 static const struct imx386_reg_list imx386_global_setting = {
